# Recovery training from placed lying starts against a hidden get-up reference (RECOVERY.md) on absolute.args.
# "StableMimic" marks a value taken from StableMimic (arXiv 2608.02385v1); every other value is this repository's choice.
@absolute.args
# StableMimic, Sections III-B and III-D: tracking and recovery starts are drawn equally often.
--recovery-share 0.5
# The get-up recordings of the 40-clip library whose rows are recovery starts and the hidden reference.
--recovery-hidden-clips fallAndGetUp1_subject1 fallAndGetUp1_subject5 fallAndGetUp2_subject2 fallAndGetUp2_subject3
    fallAndGetUp3_subject1
# No command row of a recovery start comes from a get-up recording (fallAndGetUp1_subject4 is excluded although it is
# not a hidden clip).
--recovery-command-excluded-clips fallAndGetUp1_subject1 fallAndGetUp1_subject4 fallAndGetUp1_subject5
    fallAndGetUp2_subject2 fallAndGetUp2_subject3 fallAndGetUp3_subject1
# A reference row is low below a pelvis height of 0.50 m or with the pelvis up axis tilted beyond 60 degrees (world z
# below 0.5).
--recovery-low-pelvis 0.50 0.5
# A get-up ends at the last row of its first 1 s (50 rows) of upright rows; at most 7.5 s (375 rows) from a start row
# to that end, so the blend and 1 s of command tracking fit the 10 s episode; a command row has 500 upright rows ahead
# inside its clip (the episode limit), so no clip end or low command row meets a recovery episode.
--recovery-rows 50 375 500
# StableMimic, Section III-C: the tracking terms of the get-up reference weigh 2.5 times the command's.
--recovery-reward-scale 2.5
# StableMimic, Section III-B: 2.0 s (100 controls) of target error stops a recovery episode, counted here as
# consecutive controls; a 1.5 s (75-control) transition back to the command, with a linear weight.
--recovery-controls 100 75
